1
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:46,146
[gentle music playing]

2
00:00:55,354 --> 00:00:57,771
[Ry] <i>My body has become my enemy.</i>

3
00:00:59,854 --> 00:01:03,146
<i>But here I am,
just another particle of the Earth.</i>

4
00:01:04,187 --> 00:01:07,021
<i>The ocean doesn't care about sickness</i>

5
00:01:07,104 --> 00:01:09,896
<i>or life and death.</i>

6
00:01:09,979 --> 00:01:12,812
<i>It doesn't care for
our struggles or our pain.</i>

7
00:01:14,479 --> 00:01:17,396
<i>Or that I would have given everything...</i>

8
00:01:18,687 --> 00:01:20,812
<i>...for one last summer like this.</i>

9
00:01:22,271 --> 00:01:24,354
<i>One last sunrise...</i>

10
00:01:25,646 --> 00:01:27,062
<i>...with him.</i>

11
00:01:30,187 --> 00:01:32,146
{\an8}[♪ Kye Kye sings "People"]

12
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:39,021
♪ ♪

13
00:02:01,812 --> 00:02:04,354
<i>♪ I still yearn to be ♪</i>

14
00:02:04,437 --> 00:02:07,021
<i>♪ love without a need to please ♪</i>

15
00:02:07,104 --> 00:02:08,937
<i>♪ Help me, help me ♪</i>

16
00:02:11,687 --> 00:02:15,229
{\an8}<i>♪ Silent crave to have childish peace ♪</i>

17
00:02:15,312 --> 00:02:17,021
<i>♪ while weary things ♪</i>

18
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:18,979
- [ears ringing, heart beating]
- <i>♪ haunt me, haunt me ♪</i>

19
00:02:19,062 --> 00:02:21,396
- <i>♪ Like falling in my sleep...</i>
- [breathes shakily]

20
00:02:21,479 --> 00:02:23,479
[music continues low and distorted]

21
00:02:23,562 --> 00:02:26,104
[shallow gasping]

22
00:02:27,187 --> 00:02:29,396
Ry. Ry.

23
00:02:29,479 --> 00:02:31,354
- [shallow gasping continues]
- [heart beating faster]

24
00:02:31,437 --> 00:02:34,146
[tense music playing]

25
00:02:34,229 --> 00:02:36,271
Ry!

26
00:02:36,354 --> 00:02:37,562
Move, move, move!

27
00:02:37,646 --> 00:02:39,104
I got her. Okay.

28
00:02:39,187 --> 00:02:40,229
Okay, breathe.

29
00:02:40,312 --> 00:02:42,604
Breathe, Ry.
You got to breathe, sweetheart.

30
00:02:46,062 --> 00:02:49,312
At this stage, Oriah,
I would strongly recommend surgery.

31
00:02:49,396 --> 00:02:51,729
{\an8}There's still a chance
we can remove all the tubers,

32
00:02:51,812 --> 00:02:54,271
{\an8}and you could be seizure-free.

33
00:02:54,354 --> 00:02:57,187
{\an8}And there's an equal chance
that I'll lose my memory.

34
00:02:58,521 --> 00:03:02,687
{\an8}People, places, how to walk,
how to dance, how to live.

35
00:03:02,771 --> 00:03:05,312
Everything that makes me a person.

36
00:03:05,396 --> 00:03:07,146
Ry, this is your life we're talking about.

37
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:09,896
Exactly, Mom. It's my life.

38
00:03:09,979 --> 00:03:12,062
{\an8}Okay, we could increase the medication,

39
00:03:12,146 --> 00:03:14,729
{\an8}but it'll most likely increase
the side effects.

40
00:03:14,812 --> 00:03:16,771
{\an8}I would set alarms
so you don't miss a dose,

41
00:03:16,854 --> 00:03:19,104
{\an8}or they won't work properly.

42
00:03:19,187 --> 00:03:21,104
{\an8}Can you commit to that?

43
00:03:22,771 --> 00:03:25,354
Ry. Ry.

44
00:03:28,521 --> 00:03:30,896
Honey, I know they make you
feel like shit.

45
00:03:30,979 --> 00:03:32,562
{\an8}Correction.

46
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:34,729
{\an8}They don't let me feel anything.

47
00:03:34,812 --> 00:03:36,854
All right, Lena, be sure to book a driver
to take her

48
00:03:36,937 --> 00:03:38,604
- wherever she wants to go.
- Yeah.

49
00:03:38,687 --> 00:03:41,437
Also, there's a pharmacy
two streets over from the hotel

50
00:03:41,521 --> 00:03:43,396
where you can fill her prescription.

51
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:45,104
Other than that,
it's just the usual things

52
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:46,604
{\an8}we need to be mindful of
with her epilepsy:

53
00:03:46,687 --> 00:03:48,896
{\an8}flashing lights, get good sleep,

54
00:03:48,979 --> 00:03:50,896
no stress, no alcohol.

55
00:03:50,979 --> 00:03:53,562
Great. The nuns and I will be having
our hot girl summer.

56
00:03:54,729 --> 00:03:57,021
So, days one through four are super busy

57
00:03:57,104 --> 00:03:59,437
with the location manager
and Redwyn attorneys.

58
00:03:59,521 --> 00:04:01,812
I'll try to schedule some time off, but--

59
00:04:01,896 --> 00:04:03,354
What about spending time together?

60
00:04:05,562 --> 00:04:07,187
Mom, you promised to show me
where you grew up.

61
00:04:07,271 --> 00:04:10,937
No, honey, we are gonna spend
lots of time together.

62
00:04:11,021 --> 00:04:12,396
We have six whole weeks.

63
00:04:12,479 --> 00:04:14,479
We're gonna have fun. It's Mallorca.

64
00:04:14,562 --> 00:04:16,604
As long as you keep your promise.

65
00:04:28,479 --> 00:04:30,604
Thank you.

66
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,312
All right, let me see that schedule again.

67
00:04:32,396 --> 00:04:33,604
[Lena] Yes.

68
00:04:33,687 --> 00:04:36,021
{\an8}[♪ Sofia Kourtesis sings "Madres"]

69
00:04:40,521 --> 00:04:42,479
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

70
00:04:52,646 --> 00:04:53,729
[tires screech]

71
00:04:54,771 --> 00:04:56,729
♪ ♪

72
00:05:14,271 --> 00:05:15,312
<i>Hola.</i>

73
00:05:15,396 --> 00:05:16,854
[hotel manager] Welcome.

74
00:05:18,187 --> 00:05:20,104
We're expecting you, Miss Pera.

75
00:05:20,187 --> 00:05:22,312
- Oh, call me Isolde. Hi.
- Welcome.

76
00:05:22,396 --> 00:05:24,646
<i>Muchas gracias.</i> Thank you.

77
00:05:24,729 --> 00:05:27,521
This is my daughter Oriah. Honey.

78
00:05:27,604 --> 00:05:28,812
- Hi.
- She's a bit jet-lagged.

79
00:05:28,896 --> 00:05:30,479
- Hi.
- Why don't you get settled,

80
00:05:30,562 --> 00:05:32,187
and I'll meet you in the room, okay?

81
00:05:32,271 --> 00:05:33,729
I have a quick conference call.

82
00:05:33,812 --> 00:05:35,562
[hotel manager] Our concierge team
is looking forward

83
00:05:35,646 --> 00:05:36,812
<i>- to meeting you.</i>
- [indistinct chatter]

84
00:05:39,854 --> 00:05:40,896
[Amara German accent] Hi there,

85
00:05:40,979 --> 00:05:42,229
and welcome to our hotel.

86
00:05:42,312 --> 00:05:44,479
- Hi.
- How was your flight?

87
00:05:44,562 --> 00:05:46,187
- It was fine.
- Good.

88
00:05:46,271 --> 00:05:48,604
Oh, sorry, you have a little something.

89
00:05:48,687 --> 00:05:50,187
Ah! [chuckles]

90
00:05:50,271 --> 00:05:53,062
I saw it on TikTok.
This took me 20 minutes.

91
00:05:53,146 --> 00:05:54,896
Tell me, honestly,

92
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:57,604
is it worth investing the time
on the other eye?

93
00:05:58,646 --> 00:06:01,437
Given it's company time,
I'd say yes. [chuckles]

94
00:06:01,521 --> 00:06:03,562
Mm. I like you.

95
00:06:03,646 --> 00:06:05,062
Follow me. Right,
I'll show you to your room.

96
00:06:05,146 --> 00:06:06,229
This way.

97
00:06:06,312 --> 00:06:08,146
- [Amara] I'm Amara, by the way.
- [Ry] I'm Ry.

98
00:06:08,229 --> 00:06:10,354
[Amara] Okay, so this is the lobby.

99
00:06:10,437 --> 00:06:11,812
You can come find me here
anytime you need.

100
00:06:11,896 --> 00:06:15,229
So, what brings you
to our Spanish paradise?

101
00:06:15,312 --> 00:06:17,979
- My mom's closing a real estate deal.
- Uh-huh?

102
00:06:18,062 --> 00:06:19,979
Yeah, her company wants
to build a new hotel.

103
00:06:20,062 --> 00:06:22,604
[gasps] Ooh, another hotel. How exciting.

104
00:06:22,687 --> 00:06:24,521
The locals are gonna love that.

105
00:06:24,604 --> 00:06:25,937
Do you know the island at all?

106
00:06:26,021 --> 00:06:28,187
No. No, it's my first time.

107
00:06:28,271 --> 00:06:30,062
I haven't really been out of Texas much.

108
00:06:30,146 --> 00:06:33,104
Wow, a Texan. How exotic.

109
00:06:33,187 --> 00:06:36,771
So, Ry, what do you like to do for fun?

110
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:37,979
Oh, I don't know.

111
00:06:38,062 --> 00:06:40,437
Maybe go to the beach or lie by the pool.

112
00:06:40,521 --> 00:06:43,896
You can definitely do that,
but there's tons of other stuff.

113
00:06:43,979 --> 00:06:45,896
- Do you like caves?
- Caves?

114
00:06:45,979 --> 00:06:47,146
[Amara] <i>Are you single?</i>

115
00:06:47,229 --> 00:06:49,854
- Yeah.
- Ugh, the locals here are superhot.

116
00:06:49,937 --> 00:06:52,937
They're like this crazy mix
of Carthaginians, then Romans,

117
00:06:53,021 --> 00:06:55,104
then the Catalan settlers
from France and Spain.

118
00:06:55,187 --> 00:06:58,604
Whatever you are into,
it's like a hookup buffet.

119
00:06:58,687 --> 00:07:01,521
Oh, and don't be surprised
if you see goats in trees.

120
00:07:01,604 --> 00:07:03,729
- Goats in trees?
- Yes, goats in trees.

121
00:07:03,812 --> 00:07:04,937
Anyway, the point is,

122
00:07:05,021 --> 00:07:07,521
you're going to have a summer
worth remembering.

123
00:07:07,604 --> 00:07:09,479
Okay, your mother's room
is just across the hall,

124
00:07:09,562 --> 00:07:11,562
and this one's you.

125
00:07:12,937 --> 00:07:14,937
[gentle music playing]

126
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,646
Your mother's company built
an amazing place.

127
00:07:22,104 --> 00:07:23,354
Yeah.

128
00:07:25,479 --> 00:07:27,729
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

129
00:07:27,812 --> 00:07:29,562
Sorry.

130
00:07:29,646 --> 00:07:31,562
- [alarm stops]
- I'll let you settle in.

131
00:07:31,646 --> 00:07:33,896
Just give us a call downstairs
if you need anything at all.

132
00:07:33,979 --> 00:07:35,312
<i>Auf Wiedersehen.</i> Bye-bye.

133
00:07:35,396 --> 00:07:37,771
- Thank you, Amara.
- [door closes]

134
00:07:47,687 --> 00:07:49,229
[pills rattle]

135
00:07:57,146 --> 00:07:58,312
[bottle closes]

136
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:01,854
- [waves rolling]
- [seagulls calling]

137
00:08:01,937 --> 00:08:03,854
[Ry] So, what's the plan for tomorrow?

138
00:08:03,937 --> 00:08:05,146
[Isolde] I'm packed.

139
00:08:05,229 --> 00:08:08,312
I have back-to-back meetings
and party planning.

140
00:08:09,187 --> 00:08:10,271
What party?

141
00:08:10,354 --> 00:08:12,312
A fundraiser.

142
00:08:12,396 --> 00:08:15,271
Yeah. In addition to getting them
to let us build the hotel,

143
00:08:15,354 --> 00:08:17,521
in good faith,
we are building an arts center

144
00:08:17,604 --> 00:08:20,062
- for the children of Mallorca.
- That's nice.

145
00:08:20,146 --> 00:08:21,312
[phone chimes]

146
00:08:24,062 --> 00:08:25,604
Everything okay?

147
00:08:25,687 --> 00:08:27,937
Just the-the company. [sighs]

148
00:08:28,021 --> 00:08:30,187
They're checking in
to see if I'll return this fall.

149
00:08:31,229 --> 00:08:32,812
But you are going back, right?

150
00:08:32,896 --> 00:08:34,979
You just need to rest this summer.

151
00:08:35,062 --> 00:08:36,854
And then you're gonna be
back in the saddle.

152
00:08:38,562 --> 00:08:40,229
Yeah.

153
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,479
[Chloe over phone] <i>We're all going out
tonight to celebrate</i>

154
00:08:43,562 --> 00:08:44,771
<i>the end of the season.</i>

155
00:08:44,854 --> 00:08:46,229
<i>We wish you were here.</i>

156
00:08:46,312 --> 00:08:47,604
<i>How are you feeling?</i>

157
00:08:47,687 --> 00:08:49,146
<i>Is the new medication helping?</i>

158
00:08:49,229 --> 00:08:51,979
Uh, it's... [chuckles]
it's an adjustment for sure.

159
00:08:52,062 --> 00:08:54,687
<i>We've all been so worried about you.</i>

160
00:08:54,771 --> 00:08:57,437
First of all, don't do that.

161
00:08:57,521 --> 00:08:59,271
Second, I am fine.

162
00:08:59,354 --> 00:09:02,812
My mom has this whole thing
planned for tomorrow.

163
00:09:02,896 --> 00:09:05,021
She's gonna show me where she grew up.

164
00:09:05,104 --> 00:09:06,562
<i>Your mom is such a queen.</i>

165
00:09:06,646 --> 00:09:07,646
<i>And forget what I said.</i>

166
00:09:07,729 --> 00:09:09,771
<i>I wish we were all there with you guys.</i>

167
00:09:09,854 --> 00:09:10,812
Mm-hmm.

168
00:09:10,896 --> 00:09:12,271
<i>Well, tell me
if you see any hot Spaniards.</i>

169
00:09:12,354 --> 00:09:14,021
<i>- Okay?</i>
- Yeah. For sure.

170
00:09:14,104 --> 00:09:15,771
<i>- We love you, babes. Call me!</i>
- [chuckles]

171
00:09:15,854 --> 00:09:17,771
- [women] <i>See you, Ry!
- Love you.</i>

172
00:09:17,854 --> 00:09:19,854
- Love you. Bye.
- [women] <i>Bye.</i>

173
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:25,354
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

174
00:09:25,437 --> 00:09:27,146
- [sighs]
- [alarm stops]

175
00:09:27,229 --> 00:09:29,229
[gentle guitar music playing]

176
00:09:30,312 --> 00:09:31,729
[sputters lips]

177
00:09:43,062 --> 00:09:45,021
♪ ♪

178
00:09:49,396 --> 00:09:51,354
[splashing and laughter in distance]

179
00:09:53,104 --> 00:09:56,146
[splashing and laughter continue]

180
00:09:58,021 --> 00:10:00,021
[guard] Hey! [shouts in Spanish]

181
00:10:02,396 --> 00:10:04,354
[urgent Spanish chatter]

182
00:10:10,687 --> 00:10:13,521
[birds chirping]

183
00:10:13,604 --> 00:10:16,604
[Isolde] Okay, so we have
around 150 guests.

184
00:10:16,687 --> 00:10:17,854
Ooh, this is pretty.

185
00:10:17,937 --> 00:10:22,521
Hey, Ry, do you like eggshell or oatmeal?

186
00:10:22,604 --> 00:10:24,479
Why do they all have to be
named after food?

187
00:10:24,562 --> 00:10:26,396
[Isolde] I don't know.

188
00:10:27,437 --> 00:10:29,354
[sighs] Honey, why don't you go
do something fun,

189
00:10:29,437 --> 00:10:31,437
and I'll meet up with you later.

190
00:10:32,437 --> 00:10:34,187
- I was gonna hit the beach.
- Well, that's a good idea.

191
00:10:34,271 --> 00:10:36,354
Take the driver. Oh!

192
00:10:36,437 --> 00:10:38,687
And extra meds. And water.

193
00:10:38,771 --> 00:10:40,187
And put some sunblock, sweetheart.

194
00:10:40,271 --> 00:10:42,854
- Oh, and, Ry--
- Be careful?

195
00:10:42,937 --> 00:10:44,896
Have fun.

196
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:48,229
Coconut cream for the win.

197
00:10:48,312 --> 00:10:49,937
[footsteps departing]

198
00:10:50,021 --> 00:10:52,229
See? Pretends not to care, but she does.

199
00:10:52,312 --> 00:10:53,687
Hmm.

200
00:10:57,271 --> 00:10:59,937
- Hi.
- Hi.

201
00:11:00,021 --> 00:11:01,521
Slow morning, was it?

202
00:11:01,604 --> 00:11:03,354
Why?

203
00:11:03,437 --> 00:11:04,437
[chuckles] Your eyes.

204
00:11:04,521 --> 00:11:06,062
- Oh.
- I love the eyeliner.

205
00:11:06,146 --> 00:11:07,187
- Thank you.
- [chuckles]

206
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:08,854
So, where to?

207
00:11:08,937 --> 00:11:12,812
Oh, actually, yes, I was gonna ask you
if you had any beach recommendations.

208
00:11:12,896 --> 00:11:15,437
I think I know just the spot.

209
00:11:15,521 --> 00:11:17,729
- It's a real hidden gem.
- Ooh.

210
00:11:17,812 --> 00:11:19,146
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

211
00:11:20,187 --> 00:11:21,854
Perfect.

212
00:11:21,937 --> 00:11:24,521
[♪ Bad Bunny and The Marias
sing "Otro Atardecer"]

213
00:11:34,854 --> 00:11:36,812
♪ ♪

214
00:11:43,146 --> 00:11:45,104
[quiet chatter]

215
00:11:54,396 --> 00:11:56,396
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

216
00:12:18,187 --> 00:12:20,146
♪ ♪

217
00:12:47,479 --> 00:12:49,437
♪ ♪

218
00:12:58,437 --> 00:13:00,437
[song fades]

219
00:13:05,271 --> 00:13:07,229
[quiet chatter]

220
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:35,354
[laughter in distance]

221
00:13:39,104 --> 00:13:41,104
[laughter continues]

222
00:13:45,979 --> 00:13:47,146
[sighs heavily]

223
00:13:47,229 --> 00:13:50,021
["Otro Atardecer" resumes
with lyrics in Spanish]

224
00:14:03,187 --> 00:14:04,604
[laughs]

225
00:14:06,312 --> 00:14:09,021
- [song fades]
- [laughter, quiet chatter]

226
00:14:10,062 --> 00:14:12,062
[gentle music playing]

227
00:14:36,729 --> 00:14:38,979
♪ ♪

228
00:14:51,187 --> 00:14:53,187
[music fades]

229
00:14:55,687 --> 00:14:57,687
Can I help you?

230
00:14:58,896 --> 00:15:02,437
Uh... um, no, no.

231
00:15:03,437 --> 00:15:04,646
It's rude to stare, <i>señorita.</i>

232
00:15:04,729 --> 00:15:06,271
I wasn't... I wasn't staring.

233
00:15:06,354 --> 00:15:08,187
I was just, uh, uh...

234
00:15:08,271 --> 00:15:10,187
I was looking behind you.

235
00:15:11,812 --> 00:15:14,187
[Julian] Wow. Nice view.

236
00:15:16,437 --> 00:15:18,312
[chuckles nervously]
Okay, well, I'm gonna go.

237
00:15:18,396 --> 00:15:20,562
- Yeah, you should go.
- Excuse me?

238
00:15:20,646 --> 00:15:22,937
I said that you should go.

239
00:15:23,021 --> 00:15:25,437
Did I do something?
Uh, do you have a problem?

240
00:15:25,521 --> 00:15:27,187
I do have a problem.

241
00:15:27,271 --> 00:15:29,604
This is a locals' beach.

242
00:15:29,687 --> 00:15:32,896
We prefer when tourists don't
stare at us while we sunbathe.

243
00:15:32,979 --> 00:15:34,104
Uh, I'm so sorry.

244
00:15:34,187 --> 00:15:35,271
I hadn't realized
it was a locals-only beach.

245
00:15:35,354 --> 00:15:36,396
I just wanted to swim.

246
00:15:36,479 --> 00:15:38,312
Well, I think you might find the pool

247
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:41,312
at the Marès & Mar Hotel more comfortable.

248
00:15:41,396 --> 00:15:42,437
How'd you--

249
00:15:52,021 --> 00:15:53,271
Why?

250
00:15:53,354 --> 00:15:54,604
Am I distracting you?

