- [band playing flamenco music]
- [singer speaking Spanish]

704
00:40:23,771 --> 00:40:25,937
[singing in Spanish]

705
00:40:27,396 --> 00:40:30,104
[talking indistinctly under music]

706
00:40:37,396 --> 00:40:39,437
[chef talking indistinctly under music]

707
00:40:39,521 --> 00:40:40,812
Mmm.

708
00:40:40,896 --> 00:40:42,896
[talking indistinctly under music]

709
00:40:45,104 --> 00:40:46,479
I love the artichoke.

710
00:40:48,312 --> 00:40:51,271
[conversing indistinctly under music]

711
00:40:56,437 --> 00:40:58,562
- [song continues]
- [shoes tapping rhythmically]

712
00:41:03,896 --> 00:41:05,854
[Isolde speaking Spanish]

713
00:41:09,396 --> 00:41:11,396
[talking indistinctly under music]

714
00:41:14,937 --> 00:41:17,687
- [song ends]
- [woman] <i>¡Olé! ¡Olé!</i>

715
00:41:17,771 --> 00:41:18,812
- Incredible. Oh, my--
- [song resumes]

716
00:41:18,896 --> 00:41:19,729
[singer exclaiming in Spanish]

717
00:41:19,812 --> 00:41:20,646
- Oh.
- Oh.

718
00:41:20,729 --> 00:41:21,687
Oh, my God! Our turn.

719
00:41:21,771 --> 00:41:23,646
- [laughing]
- Get it, Mom.

720
00:41:23,729 --> 00:41:25,562
[both laughing]

721
00:41:25,646 --> 00:41:27,604
[singer continues exclaiming in Spanish]

722
00:41:31,312 --> 00:41:33,312
[song fades]

723
00:41:37,229 --> 00:41:38,604
Ooh, thank God. There you are.

724
00:41:38,687 --> 00:41:41,937
Will you come with me to a bar downtown
for a Tinder date?

725
00:41:42,021 --> 00:41:43,146
[laughs] No.

726
00:41:43,229 --> 00:41:45,521
No, I can't come on a date with you.

727
00:41:45,604 --> 00:41:48,396
Yes. You have to be my safety net
in case she's a serial killer.

728
00:41:48,479 --> 00:41:50,479
You can be our third wheel.

729
00:41:50,562 --> 00:41:52,312
We'll be one big happy tricycle.

730
