00:54:45,229 --> 00:54:47,479
I'm so sorry, but...

1021
00:54:47,562 --> 00:54:48,896
it just surprise me sometimes

1022
00:54:48,979 --> 00:54:51,937
what Americans define as success.

1023
00:54:52,021 --> 00:54:53,687
What do you mean?

1024
00:54:55,021 --> 00:54:58,937
I mean, it seems like
you just work and work

1025
00:54:59,021 --> 00:55:00,979
- [chuckles]
- just to go on vacation

1026
00:55:01,062 --> 00:55:03,604
and then buy more and more and...

1027
00:55:05,021 --> 00:55:06,854
I don't know. Look at our lives here.

1028
00:55:06,937 --> 00:55:07,896
Mm-hmm.

1029
00:55:07,979 --> 00:55:09,062
Sure, we have problems,

1030
00:55:09,146 --> 00:55:12,937
but we are more than happy
with what we have.

1031
00:55:13,021 --> 00:55:14,271
What else could we want?

1032
00:55:14,354 --> 00:55:17,062
Even Miss America ended up on my boat.

1033
00:55:18,521 --> 00:55:23,146
Sometimes you just
have to enjoy what you have

1034
00:55:23,229 --> 00:55:24,979
while you have it.

1035
00:55:26,771 --> 00:55:28,312
Does that make sense?

1036
00:55:31,437 --> 00:55:33,271
More than you know.

1037
00:55:35,729 --> 00:55:37,771
Being here...

1038
00:55:39,729 --> 00:55:42,812
...this place, this summer, it's...

1039
00:55:42,896 --> 00:55:45,396
really made me think about
where I want to be.

1040
00:55:49,104 --> 00:55:51,021
Well...

1041
00:55:51,104 --> 00:55:55,687
there's never been anywhere else on Earth
I want to be than right here.

1042
00:56:08,187 --> 00:56:10,021
[whispers] Can I see your room?

1043
00:56:12,021 --> 00:56:14,604
[♪ Love Spells sings "Love Costs"]

1044
00:56:25,562 --> 00:56:27,937
<i>♪ You could never die ♪</i>

1045
00:56:29,062 --> 00:56:32,062
<i>♪ I'll always keep you alive ♪</i>

1046
00:56:33,687 --> 00:56:36,396
<i>♪ Think about you all the time ♪</i>

1047
00:56:37,896 --> 00:56:40,729
<i>♪ My security in life ♪</i>

1048
00:56:42,437 --> 00:56:44,937
<i>♪ And when I'm low ♪</i>

1049
00:56:46,312 --> 00:56:49,437
<i>♪ you get me high like coke ♪</i>

1050
00:56:50,979 --> 00:56:53,396
<i>♪ How could I let you go? ♪</i>

1051
00:56:55,312 --> 00:56:56,729
<i>♪ I'll never know ♪</i>

1052
00:56:57,771 --> 00:57:02,437
<i>♪ You could play me like a song ♪</i>

1053
00:57:02,521 --> 00:57:06,396
<i>♪ and I'll still sing along ♪</i>

1054
00:57:06,479 --> 00:57:10,021
<i>♪ The only tune I know...</i>

1055
00:57:10,104 --> 00:57:11,479
[breathing heavily]

1056
00:57:11,562 --> 00:57:14,937
<i>♪ Love you till we're bones ♪</i>

1057
00:57:16,729 --> 00:57:20,896
<i>♪ What else can I say? ♪</i>

1058
00:57:20,979 --> 00:57:25,187
<i>♪ Another time maybe ♪</i>

1059
00:57:25,271 --> 00:57:28,271
<i>♪ And I don't got the heart ♪</i>

1060
00:57:28,354 --> 00:57:32,062
<i>♪ to leave you in this way ♪</i>

1061
00:57:33,812 --> 00:57:38,104
<i>♪ Another heartbreak ♪</i>

1062
00:57:38,187 --> 00:57:42,354
<i>♪ The cycle breaks me ♪</i>

1063
00:57:42,437 --> 00:57:45,396
<i>♪ I have myself to blame ♪</i>

1064
00:57:45,479 --> 00:57:49,396
<i>♪ for hurting in this way ♪</i>

1065
00:57:49,479 --> 00:57:53,896
<i>♪ You could play me like a song ♪</i>

1066
00:57:53,979 --> 00:57:58,354
- <i>♪ and I'll still sing along ♪</i>
- [breathing heavily, moaning]

1067
00:57:58,437 --> 00:58:01,854
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

1068
00:58:02,854 --> 00:58:06,646
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

1069
00:58:11,104 --> 00:58:14,937
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

1070
00:58:19,896 --> 00:58:22,312
<i>♪ Hold you till we're bones ♪</i>

1071
00:58:22,396 --> 00:58:23,604
[song fades]

1072
00:58:27,604 --> 00:58:29,521
[Lena] Okay, um, do you mind having--

1073
00:58:29,604 --> 00:58:31,437
Oh. Hi.

1074
00:58:31,521 --> 00:58:33,229
- How are you feeling?
- Great.

1075
00:58:33,312 --> 00:58:35,229
You look radiant and happy.

1076
00:58:35,312 --> 00:58:37,562
I am.

1077
00:58:40,396 --> 00:58:41,896
Okay, I don't want to know.

1078
00:58:41,979 --> 00:58:43,312
As long as you're being safe.

1079
00:58:43,396 --> 00:58:44,729
You don't know
these Spanish boys like I do.

1080
00:58:44,812 --> 00:58:45,937
Had I stayed on this island,

1081
00:58:46,021 --> 00:58:48,104
Lord knows how many brothers
and sisters you'd have.

1082
00:58:48,187 --> 00:58:50,271
[laughs] Mom, please.

1083
00:58:50,354 --> 00:58:51,604
Uh, if you have a second,

1084
00:58:51,687 --> 00:58:53,854
I would love to talk to you
about the dance company.

1085
00:58:53,937 --> 00:58:55,812
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- [Lena] Sorry.

1086
00:58:55,896 --> 00:58:57,521
[Isolde] Oh, no,
I don't like it. That one.

1087
00:58:57,604 --> 00:58:59,021
- That one.
- Okay, okay, we'll change it.

1088
00:58:59,104 --> 00:59:01,062
Wait. Do you know the Garcias?

1089
00:59:01,146 --> 00:59:02,937
Yeah. That's the company we're buying.

1090
00:59:04,854 --> 00:59:06,812
I thought you had all the land you needed.

1091
00:59:06,896 --> 00:59:08,771
Yeah, the Garcias own
some of the most valuable docks

1092
00:59:08,854 --> 00:59:10,812
- on the island.
- And we can't build the hotel

1093
00:59:10,896 --> 00:59:12,479
unless we buy them.

1094
00:59:17,187 --> 00:59:19,021
That's the boy you're seeing?

1095
00:59:19,104 --> 00:59:20,937
A Garcia?

1096
00:59:24,271 --> 00:59:26,979
- Lena, can I get the room?
- Of course.

1097
00:59:27,062 --> 00:59:29,812
Excuse me. Would you just mind
following me and showing me...

1098
00:59:29,896 --> 00:59:31,729
- Honey, I--
- No, Mom, please don't do this.

1099
00:59:31,812 --> 00:59:33,271
I know the situation. Don't--

1100
00:59:33,354 --> 00:59:34,729
Honey, this is for the best, okay?

1101
00:59:34,812 --> 00:59:36,312
Their business is...

1102
00:59:36,396 --> 00:59:37,604
- it's over.
- No, it's not.

1103
00:59:37,687 --> 00:59:39,479
They're just waiting for a loan.
They need more time.

1104
00:59:39,562 --> 00:59:42,062
Another loan?

1105
00:59:42,146 --> 00:59:44,437
That is just gonna put them
further into debt.

1106
00:59:46,604 --> 00:59:48,562
I'm giving them independence. Okay?

1107
00:59:48,646 --> 00:59:51,187
Freedom from being trapped
inside a failing business.

1108
00:59:51,271 --> 00:59:52,771
But they're not trapped though.

1109
00:59:52,854 --> 00:59:55,562
They love it here. They love what they do.

1110
00:59:56,687 --> 01:00:00,312
To them, it's just...
it's not about money.

1111
01:00:00,396 --> 01:00:02,104
It's so much more than that.

1112
01:00:02,187 --> 01:00:03,896
It's family, and it's where they're from.

1113
01:00:03,979 --> 01:00:07,312
No, I know. I know the Garcias.

1114
01:00:07,396 --> 01:00:09,896
And I feel for them.

1115
01:00:09,979 --> 01:00:11,771
Okay? I do.

1116
01:00:11,854 --> 01:00:12,979
But between you and I,

1117
01:00:13,062 --> 01:00:15,521
I offered them double
than what it's worth.

1118
01:00:15,604 --> 01:00:16,687
I'm not the villain here.

1119
01:00:16,771 --> 01:00:19,396
Mateo Garcia is never gonna have to work
another day in his life, nor his son.

1120
01:00:19,479 --> 01:00:20,854
It's not about that.

1121
01:00:20,937 --> 01:00:22,812
This is what makes them happy.

1122
01:00:22,896 --> 01:00:25,396
Mom, this gives them purpose.

1123
01:00:28,396 --> 01:00:31,687
[chuckles] You know,
it's easy to be idealistic, okay?

1124
01:00:31,771 --> 01:00:34,187
But business is business.
It's-it's not personal.

1125
01:00:36,187 --> 01:00:38,021
Please.

1126
01:00:39,979 --> 01:00:41,437
Please.

1127
01:00:43,229 --> 01:00:44,937
For me.

1128
01:00:46,854 --> 01:00:50,271
Okay, look, I'll see what I can do,
but I'm not promising anything, okay?

1129
01:00:54,146 --> 01:00:59,104
- [♪ Esha Tewari sings "In Twos"]
- <i>♪ I'll catch the train again ♪</i>

1130
01:00:59,187 --> 01:01:03,729
<i>♪ Starry-eyed
and I'm stalking your mind...</i>

1131
01:01:03,812 --> 01:01:05,604
Can I talk to you about something?

1132
01:01:07,896 --> 01:01:12,479
<i>♪ The light that you lead home ♪</i>

1133
01:01:12,562 --> 01:01:13,646
<i>♪ Drink a jug...</i>

1134
01:01:13,729 --> 01:01:18,437
Can we just have one day
where we forget it all?

1135
01:01:18,521 --> 01:01:19,646
Please?

1136
01:01:21,646 --> 01:01:22,812
- Yeah.
- [song ends]

1137
01:01:22,896 --> 01:01:25,187
[uplifting music playing]

1138
01:01:52,646 --> 01:01:54,604
♪ ♪

1139
01:01:59,396 --> 01:02:01,396
- [Isolde] Ry, sweetie?
- [knock on door]

1140
01:02:01,479 --> 01:02:03,104
Are you here? Hey.

1141
01:02:03,187 --> 01:02:07,437
I have meetings all day,
but I wanted to see you before I left.

1142
01:02:07,521 --> 01:02:09,437
Did you refill your meds? Oh.

1143
01:02:09,521 --> 01:02:12,854
I got you two dresses,
this green and pink,

1144
01:02:12,937 --> 01:02:15,312
so let me know which one
you want to wear to the fundraiser.

1145
01:02:15,396 --> 01:02:18,146
Did you figure something out
for the Garcias?

1146
01:02:18,229 --> 01:02:21,562
Not yet, but I am working on it, okay?

1147
01:02:21,646 --> 01:02:22,812
[knock on door]

1148
01:02:22,896 --> 01:02:24,396
[Lena] Sorry, we're running late.

1149
01:02:24,479 --> 01:02:25,437
Yeah, here.

1150
01:02:25,521 --> 01:02:28,104
I'm gonna be busy today,
but why don't we have breakfast tomorrow.

1151
01:02:29,437 --> 01:02:31,479
You feeling okay?

1152
01:02:31,562 --> 01:02:33,604
You look a little pale.

1153
01:02:33,687 --> 01:02:35,146
I'm good.

1154
01:02:36,187 --> 01:02:38,229
Okay. I love you.

1155
01:02:38,312 --> 01:02:40,062
See you later.

1156
01:02:40,146 --> 01:02:42,146
[door opens, closes]

1157
01:02:43,187 --> 01:02:44,562
[phone chimes and vibrates]

1158
01:02:51,271 --> 01:02:53,229
[gentle music playing]

1159
01:02:54,687 --> 01:02:56,229
[Julian] <i>Do you trust me?</i>

1160
01:02:57,312 --> 01:02:58,562
Yeah.

1161
01:03:00,562 --> 01:03:02,437
Turn off the light.

1162
01:03:05,229 --> 01:03:06,271
Okay.

1163
01:03:15,979 --> 01:03:19,854
This... is my favorite feeling.

1164
01:03:21,146 --> 01:03:24,271
You just melt into everything around you.

1165
01:03:25,312 --> 01:03:28,396
It helps me forget about the problems
when the lights are on.

1166
01:03:31,812 --> 01:03:34,812
It's good to face your fears, Oriah.

1167
01:03:37,354 --> 01:03:39,854
How else can you overcome them?

1168
01:03:39,937 --> 01:03:41,937
♪ ♪

1169
01:03:50,187 --> 01:03:52,396
[♪ Levitation Room sings "Pienso en Ti"]

1170
01:03:52,479 --> 01:03:54,479
[seagulls squawking]

1171
01:04:00,187 --> 01:04:02,729
This is where we met. [chuckles]

1172
01:04:05,104 --> 01:04:06,312
Wait here.

1173
01:04:06,396 --> 01:04:08,396
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

1174
01:04:21,021 --> 01:04:23,187
If you can't swim, I can help you.

1175
01:04:23,271 --> 01:04:24,562
[Julian chuckles]

1176
01:04:32,104 --> 01:04:34,104
♪ ♪

1177
01:04:50,562 --> 01:04:52,479
- [song fades]
- [phone ringing and vibrating]

1178
01:04:52,562 --> 01:04:54,604
[chuckles]

1179
01:04:54,687 --> 01:04:56,062
Hey.

1180
01:04:56,146 --> 01:04:58,146
[Chloe over phone] <i>Why do you look
like you just got laid?</i>

1181
01:04:58,229 --> 01:05:00,562
- [Ry laughs]
<i>- Okay, spill the tea.</i>

1182
01:05:00,646 --> 01:05:02,979
Let's just say we have
a lot of catching up to do.

1183
01:05:03,062 --> 01:05:04,854
<i>What is happening on that island?</i>

1184
01:05:04,937 --> 01:05:06,771
<i>Tell me everything.</i>

1185
01:05:06,854 --> 01:05:08,729
Dude, I think I'm in love.

1186
01:05:09,854 --> 01:05:12,646
[chuckles] Like, on a cellular level.

1187
01:05:12,729 --> 01:05:16,062
<i>On a cell-- Who even are you right now?</i>

1188
01:05:16,146 --> 01:05:17,771
- [laughs]
<i>- Okay, what-what are you gonna do?</i>

1189
01:05:17,854 --> 01:05:20,437
<i>Aren't you coming home
in a couple of days?</i>

1190
01:05:21,521 --> 01:05:22,562
I don't know.

1191
01:05:22,646 --> 01:05:23,979
<i>Wow.</i>

1192
01:05:24,062 --> 01:05:25,812
<i>So this is serious?</i>

1193
01:05:25,896 --> 01:05:27,771
Romeo and Juliet serious.

1194
01:05:27,854 --> 01:05:29,562
<i>Wait, didn't one of them die?</i>

1195
01:05:29,646 --> 01:05:31,396
- [knock on door]
- [Lena] Hey, it's Lena.

1196
01:05:31,479 --> 01:05:33,729
- I have to go.
- [Chloe] <i>Okay, talk soon. Call me.</i>

1197
01:05:33,812 --> 01:05:35,021
Yeah?

1198
01:05:36,396 --> 01:05:38,562
Hi, Ry. Your mom's
not gonna make it this morning.

1199
01:05:38,646 --> 01:05:40,104
- [door closes]
- With the event tonight,

1200
01:05:40,187 --> 01:05:42,604
she's being pulled
in a million directions.

1201
01:05:42,687 --> 01:05:44,979
Look, I know it's not my place to say...

1202
01:05:46,021 --> 01:05:47,521
but...

1203
01:05:47,604 --> 01:05:49,937
the Garcias have agreed to sell.

1204
01:05:51,521 --> 01:05:53,729
They're signing with Redwyn now.

1205
01:05:54,854 --> 01:05:56,646
- What?
- I'm so sorry, Ry.

1206
01:05:56,729 --> 01:05:57,729
I have to go.

1207
01:05:57,812 --> 01:05:59,771
[line ringing]

1208
01:05:59,854 --> 01:06:02,062
[Julian speaking Spanish
in voicemail recording]

1209
01:06:02,146 --> 01:06:03,354
[phone beeps]

1210
01:06:04,437 --> 01:06:06,437
[panting]

1211
01:06:08,479 --> 01:06:09,479
[grunts]

1212
01:06:09,562 --> 01:06:11,562
[tense music playing]

1213
01:06:18,854 --> 01:06:20,729
No.

1214
01:06:20,812 --> 01:06:21,937
[exhales sharply]

1215
01:06:32,396 --> 01:06:33,646
Julian!

1216
01:06:34,729 --> 01:06:36,812
Julian, what happened?

1217
01:06:37,896 --> 01:06:39,729
Who did this?

1218
01:06:39,812 --> 01:06:41,937
It was Carlos.

1219
01:06:42,021 --> 01:06:43,437
Last night.

1220
01:06:45,062 --> 01:06:46,271
Now my father...

1221
01:06:48,646 --> 01:06:50,479
It was the final straw.

1222
01:06:51,479 --> 01:06:53,562
He signed with Redwyn.

1223
01:07:00,396 --> 01:07:01,562
It's all my fault.

1224
01:07:05,021 --> 01:07:06,312
No.

1225
01:07:08,354 --> 01:07:09,521
No, it's not.

1226
01:07:14,646 --> 01:07:16,312
Julian, my mom works for Redwyn.

1227
01:07:22,854 --> 01:07:24,312
I'm so sorry. I just found out--

1228
01:07:24,396 --> 01:07:25,979
You need to leave, Ry.

1229
01:07:26,062 --> 01:07:28,479
- What? But I just--
- Leave!

1230
01:07:28,562 --> 01:07:29,729
Leave.

1231
01:07:37,062 --> 01:07:38,604
[sniffles]

1232
01:07:39,604 --> 01:07:41,229
Mom?

1233
01:07:41,312 --> 01:07:42,646
Mom, what happened?

1234
01:07:42,729 --> 01:07:45,479
Could you give me a moment? Thank you.

1235
01:07:45,562 --> 01:07:47,396
You promised you would help them.

1236
01:07:47,479 --> 01:07:48,812
Honey, I did.

1237
01:07:48,896 --> 01:07:51,187
They had a sinking business,
and I threw them a lifeline.

1238
01:07:51,271 --> 01:07:53,479
[chuckles] Oh, so now
they have money and things

1239
01:07:53,562 --> 01:07:55,271
and no pride and no roots, just like you.

1240
01:07:55,354 --> 01:07:56,562
What does that mean?

1241
01:07:56,646 --> 01:07:58,979
It means you measure everything
with money.

1242
01:07:59,062 --> 01:08:01,979
You love power.
You're this power suit boss.

1243
01:08:02,062 --> 01:08:04,187
[stammers] You brought me
to where you're from,

1244
01:08:04,271 --> 01:08:06,479
and you've barely left the hotel.

1245
01:08:08,562 --> 01:08:10,354
Why do you even do all of this?

1246
01:08:11,937 --> 01:08:13,646
Why?

1247
01:08:13,729 --> 01:08:16,312
Why do I do this? I do this for you.

1248
01:08:18,062 --> 01:08:20,062
How do you not see that?

1249
01:08:20,146 --> 01:08:22,271
You think I like being busy all the time?

1250
01:08:22,354 --> 01:08:25,479
Of course I want to spend time with you.

1251
01:08:25,562 --> 01:08:28,396
But I also thank God every day
that I have this job,

1252
01:08:28,479 --> 01:08:30,562
which I'm really good at,

1253
01:08:30,646 --> 01:08:32,521
because that means
I can take care of you, Ry.

1254
01:08:32,604 --> 01:08:35,271
In every way that you need.

1255
01:08:38,729 --> 01:08:40,146
You're my purpose.

1256
01:08:41,229 --> 01:08:42,396
Okay? So...

1257
01:08:43,937 --> 01:08:45,979
If I could've changed
the outcome for the Garcias,

1258
01:08:46,062 --> 01:08:47,396
I would have.

1259
01:08:48,896 --> 01:08:50,354
Believe me, I would have.

1260
01:08:54,437 --> 01:08:55,521
[sighs]

1261
01:08:55,604 --> 01:08:58,187
So let's... let's just
take a deep breath...

1262
01:08:59,937 --> 01:09:02,479
...and get ready for the gala.

1263
01:09:02,562 --> 01:09:05,187
It is such an important night.

1264
01:09:05,271 --> 01:09:08,521
We only have a few days left here,
and I need you.

1265
01:09:09,812 --> 01:09:11,812
[pensive music playing]

1266
01:09:14,062 --> 01:09:15,562
[sighs]

1267
01:09:21,229 --> 01:09:22,562
[exhales heavily]

1268
01:09:22,646 --> 01:09:24,646
[taking off shoes]

1269
01:09:30,896 --> 01:09:31,896
[sniffles]

1270
01:09:38,104 --> 01:09:39,479
[inhales sharply]

1271
01:09:39,562 --> 01:09:41,354
[sighs]

1272
01:09:48,479 --> 01:09:49,604
[exhales shakily]

1273
01:09:49,687 --> 01:09:51,104
[whimpers]

1274
01:09:55,729 --> 01:09:57,104
[sobbing]

1275
01:10:01,812 --> 01:10:03,229
[sniffles]

1276
01:10:04,937 --> 01:10:06,937
♪ ♪

1277
01:10:23,979 --> 01:10:25,229
Oh.

1278
01:10:26,437 --> 01:10:28,604
I know you were having,
like, a super intense

1279
01:10:28,687 --> 01:10:30,562
mirror stare-off thing with yourself,

1280
01:10:30,646 --> 01:10:34,896
but for the record, you look hot.

1281
01:10:36,354 --> 01:10:39,521
And none of this is your fault,
by the way.

1282
01:10:39,604 --> 01:10:42,646
This is just the way the world works.

1283
01:10:42,729 --> 01:10:45,354
If it wasn't you guys,
it would've just been somebody else.

1284
01:10:45,437 --> 01:10:47,187
- [sighs]
- Hmm?

1285
01:10:47,271 --> 01:10:48,687
[whispers] Probably uglier.

1286
01:10:49,812 --> 01:10:52,729
- [laughs]
- Julian will come around.

1287
01:10:52,812 --> 01:10:54,687
[whispers] I promise.

1288
01:10:54,771 --> 01:10:57,687
[band playing "Tangos de la Juderia"]

1289
01:10:57,771 --> 01:10:59,771
- [lively chatter]
- [music continues]

1290
01:11:07,271 --> 01:11:09,271
[Isolde talking indistinctly under music]

1291
01:11:11,187 --> 01:11:13,104
♪ ♪

1292
01:11:13,187 --> 01:11:15,187
[indistinct chatter continues]

1293
01:11:19,271 --> 01:11:21,271
[insects trilling]

1294
01:11:23,979 --> 01:11:25,562
[sighs]

1295
01:11:35,312 --> 01:11:36,479
No.

1296
01:11:37,812 --> 01:11:39,104
Fucking chemicals.

1297
01:11:39,187 --> 01:11:40,396
[grunts]

1298
01:11:40,479 --> 01:11:42,479
[panting]

1299
01:11:46,146 --> 01:11:47,979
[calling whistle]

1300
01:11:48,062 --> 01:11:50,062
[speaking Catalan]

1301
01:11:53,396 --> 01:11:55,562
What do you want?

1302
01:11:55,646 --> 01:11:57,521
You know...

1303
01:11:57,604 --> 01:11:59,521
your boyfriend... [smacks lips]

1304
01:11:59,604 --> 01:12:00,979
he owes me a lot of money.

1305
01:12:02,187 --> 01:12:04,604
And since you seem so fond
of his beautiful face,

1306
01:12:04,687 --> 01:12:07,562
I thought you'd like to stop me
from ruining it, no?

1307
01:12:08,646 --> 01:12:09,771
You'll get your money.

1308
01:12:09,854 --> 01:12:12,604
Slow down, <i>reina.</i>

1309
01:12:12,687 --> 01:12:15,229
Not everything has to be about cash.

1310
01:12:15,312 --> 01:12:17,687
- Some things are worth more than money.
- [whimpers]

1311
01:12:17,771 --> 01:12:19,896
Like food, wine, women.

1312
01:12:19,979 --> 01:12:21,354
Get off of me.

1313
01:12:22,687 --> 01:12:24,312
[panting]

1314
01:12:24,396 --> 01:12:26,854
If you touch her again, I'll kill you.

1315
01:12:26,937 --> 01:12:28,187
You understand?

1316
01:12:31,771 --> 01:12:33,729
Your money.

1317
01:12:38,187 --> 01:12:39,562
Shame.

1318
01:12:39,646 --> 01:12:41,437
She would have been fun.

1319
01:12:44,687 --> 01:12:46,104
Now get the fuck out of here!

1320
01:12:46,187 --> 01:12:48,729
You've got no reason
to come near us again.

1321
01:12:48,812 --> 01:12:49,896
Sure.

1322
01:12:49,979 --> 01:12:51,937
Until next time.

1323
01:12:52,021 --> 01:12:53,937
[laughs]

1324
01:12:55,479 --> 01:12:57,562
- You okay? You okay?
- I'm okay.

1325
01:12:57,646 --> 01:12:59,521
- You sure?
- I'm okay. I'm okay.

1326
01:12:59,604 --> 01:13:01,021
I'm okay.

1327
01:13:04,021 --> 01:13:05,354
Nice slap, by the way.

1328
01:13:05,437 --> 01:13:07,354
[both laughing]

1329
01:13:07,437 --> 01:13:10,062
Remind me to never make you mad.

1330
01:13:10,146 --> 01:13:11,354
[chuckles]

1331
01:13:16,062 --> 01:13:18,896
I'm really sorry about
not telling you about my mom.

1332
01:13:19,896 --> 01:13:21,812
I really thought I could fix it.

1333
01:13:21,896 --> 01:13:23,354
[quietly] It's okay.

1334
01:13:23,437 --> 01:13:25,104
It's not your fault.

1335
01:13:27,604 --> 01:13:29,604
[gentle music playing]

1336
01:13:38,021 --> 01:13:39,646
- [laughs]
- [chuckles]

1337
01:13:41,354 --> 01:13:42,396
Your dress.

1338
01:13:44,021 --> 01:13:45,229
It's ruined.

1339
01:13:46,812 --> 01:13:49,687
[chuckles] I was passing on
your ecological complaint.

1340
01:13:49,771 --> 01:13:50,979
[Julian chuckles]

1341
01:13:51,062 --> 01:13:53,354
That whole thing about the grass
and the chemicals.

1342
01:13:53,437 --> 01:13:54,646
- Wow.
- [laughs]

1343
01:14:03,562 --> 01:14:05,979
- [Julian] I need you now.
- [moans]

1344
01:14:09,896 --> 01:14:12,021
♪ ♪

1345
01:14:12,104 --> 01:14:14,021
[grunting]

1346
01:14:14,104 --> 01:14:16,396
[music tempo quickens]

1347
01:14:16,479 --> 01:14:17,396
[Ry exhales heavily]

1348
01:14:24,646 --> 01:14:25,812
[Julian chuckles]

1349
01:14:29,646 --> 01:14:31,646
[breathing heavily]

1350
01:14:37,271 --> 01:14:38,979
- [grunts]
- [sighs]

1351
01:14:42,937 --> 01:14:44,812
[breathing heavily]

1352
01:14:46,729 --> 01:14:48,062
[moaning]

1353
01:14:59,979 --> 01:15:01,896
[Isolde speaking indistinctly]

1354
01:15:01,979 --> 01:15:03,437
[lively chatter and music]

1355
01:15:08,312 --> 01:15:09,479
[speaking Spanish]

1356
01:15:11,979 --> 01:15:13,187
[Amara] Cheers.

1357
01:15:16,396 --> 01:15:17,562
- [phone vibrates]
- [scoffs softly]

1358
01:15:20,437 --> 01:15:23,729
[♪ Buscabulla sings "Tártaro"]

1359
01:15:23,812 --> 01:15:25,229
[Amara] Yeah.

1360
01:15:25,312 --> 01:15:28,521
It never ceases to amaze
what rich people will leave behind.

1361
01:15:28,604 --> 01:15:30,437
That lost and found is a treasure trove.

1362
01:15:30,521 --> 01:15:32,646
How do I look?

1363
01:15:32,729 --> 01:15:34,771
[laughs]

1364
01:15:37,812 --> 01:15:39,729
I'll see you guys down there.

1365
01:15:39,812 --> 01:15:41,437
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

1366
01:15:47,896 --> 01:15:49,896
♪ ♪

1367
01:15:55,937 --> 01:15:57,437
I'm just wondering if there's a way.

1368
01:15:57,521 --> 01:15:59,604
I agree, but I'm worried
that it's too late.

1369
01:15:59,687 --> 01:16:02,021
You ready?

1370
01:16:02,104 --> 01:16:03,521
Let's do it.

1371
01:16:04,521 --> 01:16:06,104
[Ry] Mom?

1372
01:16:06,187 --> 01:16:09,896
I want to introduce you to Julian Garcia.

1373
01:16:09,979 --> 01:16:12,646
It's a pleasure to meet you, <i>Señora Pera.</i>

1374
01:16:12,729 --> 01:16:14,479
I've heard a lot about you.

1375
01:16:16,396 --> 01:16:18,396
Let me get you both a drink.

1376
01:16:24,771 --> 01:16:28,271
Did you tell him who I am
and my association with Redwyn?

1377
01:16:28,354 --> 01:16:30,146
[softly] Yeah.

1378
01:16:31,604 --> 01:16:34,354
Did you tell him about your epilepsy?

1379
01:16:42,062 --> 01:16:43,771
<i>Gracias.</i>

1380
01:16:43,854 --> 01:16:46,354
[applause]

1381
01:16:46,437 --> 01:16:48,646
<i>Buenas noches.</i> Good evening.

1382
01:16:48,729 --> 01:16:52,146
Thank you all for-for being here with us
to celebrate

1383
01:16:52,229 --> 01:16:55,521
this exciting new chapter for Mallorca.

1384
01:16:55,604 --> 01:16:59,521
We are thrilled to introduce
an arts center that will

1385
01:16:59,604 --> 01:17:03,229
preserve the cultural heartbeat
of this beautiful island.

1386
01:17:03,312 --> 01:17:07,104
Now, some of you know I grew up here,
a long time ago,

1387
01:17:07,187 --> 01:17:10,812
so it's nice to have a chance
to be able to give back,

1388
01:17:10,896 --> 01:17:14,854
and not only with this amazing arts center

1389
01:17:14,937 --> 01:17:18,896
but by bringing
a world-class resort to Mallorca.

1390
01:17:18,979 --> 01:17:22,771
So let's raise a glass

1391
01:17:22,854 --> 01:17:24,396
and make a...

1392
01:17:27,687 --> 01:17:30,187
...and let's make a toast.

1393
01:17:30,271 --> 01:17:31,896
To Mallorca.

1394
01:17:31,979 --> 01:17:34,437
[crowd] To Mallorca.

1395
01:17:34,521 --> 01:17:36,437
[applause]

1396
01:17:36,521 --> 01:17:38,521
[lively chatter]

1397
01:17:40,229 --> 01:17:42,229
[band playing gentle guitar music]

1398
01:17:48,604 --> 01:17:49,729
Mateo.

1399
01:17:49,812 --> 01:17:51,146
<i>¿Cómo estás?</i>

1400
01:17:54,729 --> 01:17:56,729
It's really good to see you.

1401
01:17:58,604 --> 01:18:00,979
I never thought I would see you again.

1402
01:18:02,354 --> 01:18:03,771
It's been a long time.

1403
01:18:04,771 --> 01:18:06,187
Yes.

1404
01:18:08,812 --> 01:18:11,771
Um, look, I want to...

1405
01:18:11,854 --> 01:18:13,729
let you know that
none of this was personal.

1406
01:18:13,812 --> 01:18:15,979
Isolde...

1407
01:18:16,062 --> 01:18:18,812
everything between us is personal.

1408
01:18:19,896 --> 01:18:21,604
[chuckles softly]

1409
01:18:21,687 --> 01:18:24,812
I mean, I just want
to explain my intentions.

1410
01:18:24,896 --> 01:18:25,937
You don't need to explain anything.

1411
01:18:26,021 --> 01:18:28,271
I mean, you're right.

1412
01:18:28,354 --> 01:18:31,771
The island is changing,
and I can't keep it up anyways.

1413
01:18:31,854 --> 01:18:33,271
I tried.

1414
01:18:34,271 --> 01:18:36,979
I held on to my business
as long as I could.

1415
01:18:38,146 --> 01:18:39,937
But in the end...

1416
01:18:43,937 --> 01:18:46,687
- I just have one thing to ask of you.
- Yeah?

1417
01:18:46,771 --> 01:18:50,896
When you're building the hotel,
when you're shaping what comes next,

1418
01:18:50,979 --> 01:18:52,979
just don't forget about
what was here before.

1419
01:18:54,979 --> 01:18:57,396
I could never forget what was here before.

1420
01:18:58,687 --> 01:19:01,729
There is one good thing to come of this.

1421
01:19:03,062 --> 01:19:07,104
Maybe they will have the future
we never could.

1422
01:19:15,437 --> 01:19:17,062
Let's go.

1423
01:19:17,146 --> 01:19:19,479
This suit makes me feel like
I'm in a straitjacket.

1424
01:19:19,562 --> 01:19:20,729
[Ry chuckles]

1425
01:19:20,812 --> 01:19:22,687
[speaks Catalan]

1426
01:19:22,771 --> 01:19:24,312
Go be with your dad.

1427
01:19:24,396 --> 01:19:26,396
I'll find you later at the docks.

1428
01:19:27,854 --> 01:19:29,521
- See you later.
- Bye.

1429
01:19:30,521 --> 01:19:32,479
[gentle guitar music playing in distance]

1430
01:19:37,812 --> 01:19:42,187
I thought you said your stories about
growing up here would bore me.

1431
01:19:50,187 --> 01:19:51,896
[Isolde inhales deeply]

1432
01:19:51,979 --> 01:19:53,729
Mateo Garcia.

1433
01:19:53,812 --> 01:19:54,937
[Ry chuckles]

1434
01:19:55,021 --> 01:19:57,146
He was my first love.

1435
01:19:57,229 --> 01:20:01,812
We met when we were kids,
and as teenagers we couldn't...

1436
01:20:01,896 --> 01:20:03,896
stay away from each other.

1437
01:20:05,937 --> 01:20:10,312
He was the air I breathed
and the water I swam in.

1438
01:20:10,396 --> 01:20:12,146
[both chuckle]

1439
01:20:12,229 --> 01:20:15,687
We always talked about the future,
and we made plans and...

1440
01:20:19,021 --> 01:20:21,437
And then everything changed.

1441
01:20:22,479 --> 01:20:23,937
Your mom died.

1442
01:20:25,854 --> 01:20:29,354
I had never experienced a pain like that.

1443
01:20:32,187 --> 01:20:35,354
And every part of the island
just reminded me of her.

1444
01:20:38,604 --> 01:20:40,187
I had to leave. I had to escape.

1445
01:20:40,271 --> 01:20:42,896
Just wanted to get away. [sniffles]

1446
01:20:42,979 --> 01:20:44,479
I asked him to come with me.

1447
01:20:44,562 --> 01:20:46,271
I begged him.

1448
01:20:46,354 --> 01:20:47,479
[chuckles softly]

1449
01:20:48,854 --> 01:20:52,271
He didn't want to leave his family
or the business.

1450
01:20:54,646 --> 01:20:58,229
We wrote letters for years,
back and forth,

1451
01:20:58,312 --> 01:21:00,104
and then one day the letters stopped.

1452
01:21:06,812 --> 01:21:09,812
So when I found out
we were building this hotel

1453
01:21:09,896 --> 01:21:13,354
and buying the land,
I jumped at the chance to help him.

1454
01:21:15,687 --> 01:21:18,354
I wish you would have told me.

1455
01:21:18,437 --> 01:21:19,771
Yeah.

1456
01:21:19,854 --> 01:21:24,021
And now I'm just the face
that stole his family's dreams.

1457
01:21:24,104 --> 01:21:25,896
No. No.

1458
01:21:31,021 --> 01:21:34,021
- You did your best, Mom.
- [scoffs softly]

1459
01:21:34,104 --> 01:21:35,771
And he knows it.

1460
01:21:35,854 --> 01:21:37,021
Yeah.

1461
01:21:37,104 --> 01:21:39,812
[♪ Barzin sings "All the While"]

1462
01:21:42,312 --> 01:21:44,854
<i>♪ All summer ♪</i>

1463
01:21:44,937 --> 01:21:47,271
<i>♪ your love burned alone...</i>

1464
01:21:49,021 --> 01:21:51,396
Can we stay up tonight?

1465
01:21:51,479 --> 01:21:52,646
Mm-hmm.

1466
01:21:53,896 --> 01:21:55,521
I've never seen a sunrise.

1467
01:21:56,937 --> 01:21:59,146
- What do you mean?
- [chuckles]

1468
01:21:59,229 --> 01:22:00,354
From the water?

1469
01:22:01,604 --> 01:22:02,896
[whispers] From anywhere.

1470
01:22:05,396 --> 01:22:06,812
Well...

1471
01:22:08,396 --> 01:22:11,062
...I can get you
the best seat in the house.

1472
01:22:11,146 --> 01:22:13,854
- Hmm?
- Mm-hmm.

1473
01:22:13,937 --> 01:22:17,396
<i>♪ Beside the girl ♪</i>

1474
01:22:19,729 --> 01:22:22,604
<i>♪ Did you wait for ♪</i>

1475
01:22:22,687 --> 01:22:25,437
<i>♪ something to change you? ♪</i>

1476
01:22:28,521 --> 01:22:31,729
<i>♪ All the while you wait ♪</i>

1477
01:22:31,812 --> 01:22:33,604
<i>♪ for your heart ♪</i>

1478
01:22:36,854 --> 01:22:40,021
<i>♪ All the while you wait ♪</i>

1479
01:22:40,104 --> 01:22:43,312
<i>♪ for your heart to... ♪</i>

1480
01:22:43,396 --> 01:22:44,521
Look.

1481
01:22:44,604 --> 01:22:46,229
<i>♪ Wake up...</i>

1482
01:22:47,562 --> 01:22:48,604
[gasps]

1483
01:22:48,687 --> 01:22:51,354
- <i>♪ For your heart ♪</i>
- [chuckles]

1484
01:22:51,437 --> 01:22:54,562
<i>♪ to wake up ♪</i>

1485
01:22:56,021 --> 01:22:59,396
Thank you for saving
your first sunrise for me.

1486
01:23:01,687 --> 01:23:04,729
You can have all my firsts
and all my lasts.

1487
01:23:04,812 --> 01:23:06,771
♪ ♪

1488
01:23:17,437 --> 01:23:18,812
[chuckles]

1489
01:23:21,271 --> 01:23:22,479
[sighs]

1490
01:23:28,979 --> 01:23:30,479
[exhales softly]

1491
01:23:30,562 --> 01:23:32,812
[song fades]

1492
01:23:38,062 --> 01:23:39,771
Mom, is everything okay?

1493
01:23:40,937 --> 01:23:43,187
When did you stop taking your meds?

1494
01:23:50,604 --> 01:23:53,062
A few days after we arrived.

1495
01:23:56,687 --> 01:23:58,312
They made me feel numb.

1496
01:23:58,396 --> 01:24:00,771
Mom, I needed a single summer
of feeling something.

1497
01:24:00,854 --> 01:24:01,854
I'm such an idiot.

1498
01:24:01,937 --> 01:24:03,312
I should have never left you alone.

1499
01:24:03,396 --> 01:24:05,021
- Stop. No.
- I should've stayed on top of you...

1500
01:24:05,104 --> 01:24:06,687
- It's my decision!
- ...to make sure you took your pills!

1501
01:24:06,771 --> 01:24:08,479
No. It's my decision.

1502
01:24:08,562 --> 01:24:10,646
You probably made everything worse!

1503
01:24:10,729 --> 01:24:13,437
[voice breaking] I don't care.
I don't care.

1504
01:24:13,521 --> 01:24:14,687
- I care.
- I don't.

1505
01:24:14,771 --> 01:24:16,104
Okay.

1506
01:24:16,187 --> 01:24:18,354
- What are you doing?
- Let's go. We're leaving.

1507
01:24:18,437 --> 01:24:19,604
No, no, we're not.

1508
01:24:19,687 --> 01:24:22,021
- We're leaving.
- No. No, please.

1509
01:24:22,104 --> 01:24:23,771
Mom, I saw the sun rise
for the first time.

1510
01:24:23,854 --> 01:24:25,396
You did? That's great.

1511
01:24:25,479 --> 01:24:27,187
I can feel things.
I can feel Julian touching me,

1512
01:24:27,271 --> 01:24:30,312
and I could feel the sea on my skin.

1513
01:24:30,396 --> 01:24:33,687
[laughs] At least there's something
worth remembering.

1514
01:24:35,771 --> 01:24:38,271
[sobs] I want to stay here.

1515
01:24:40,312 --> 01:24:42,479
I want to live.

1516
01:24:43,521 --> 01:24:45,687
You want to stay here?

1517
01:24:45,771 --> 01:24:48,062
Oh, you want to live.
Now you want to live.

1518
01:24:48,146 --> 01:24:51,062
For how long, Ry?
How long do you want to live?

1519
01:24:52,104 --> 01:24:53,521
We're leaving.

1520
01:24:53,604 --> 01:24:55,271
I told Lena to move up our flight.

1521
01:24:56,604 --> 01:24:57,729
No.

1522
01:24:57,812 --> 01:24:59,146
Pack your stuff, Ry. Let's go.

1523
01:24:59,229 --> 01:25:01,062
No, Mom.

1524
01:25:01,146 --> 01:25:02,271
No.

1525
01:25:02,354 --> 01:25:03,687
Ry!

1526
01:25:04,729 --> 01:25:06,437
- [panting]
- [tense music playing]

1527
01:25:07,479 --> 01:25:08,937
- [muffled] Ry!
- [heart beating rapidly]

1528
01:25:09,021 --> 01:25:10,146
Ry?

1529
01:25:10,229 --> 01:25:11,562
[audio continues distorted]

1530
01:25:11,646 --> 01:25:13,646
Ry, where are you going?

1531
01:25:15,146 --> 01:25:16,354
[gasping]

1532
01:25:16,437 --> 01:25:18,937
Ry? Ry!

1533
01:25:19,021 --> 01:25:21,729
[heart beating faster]

1534
01:25:21,812 --> 01:25:24,646
[whimpering]

1535
01:25:24,729 --> 01:25:27,896
- [grunting]
- [ears ringing]

1536
01:25:32,687 --> 01:25:34,521
Ry!

1537
01:25:37,812 --> 01:25:39,771
♪ ♪

1538
01:26:02,021 --> 01:26:03,896
- [Isolde] <i>Move, move, move! Ry!</i>
- [water rushing]

1539
01:26:03,979 --> 01:26:05,062
[audio continues clearly]

1540
01:26:05,146 --> 01:26:06,229
Hey, hey, hey. Shh.

1541
01:26:06,312 --> 01:26:08,729
It's okay. You're okay, baby. You're okay.

1542
01:26:08,812 --> 01:26:11,021
I'm right here. I'm right here.

1543
01:26:11,104 --> 01:26:12,979
Everything's gonna be okay.

1544
01:26:13,062 --> 01:26:14,771
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1545
01:26:14,854 --> 01:26:15,979
[whispers] I'm here.

1546
01:26:16,062 --> 01:26:17,854
[chuckles] There you are.

1547
01:26:18,896 --> 01:26:20,854
[crickets chirping]

1548
01:26:20,937 --> 01:26:23,312
- [breathlessly] Hi.
- [Isolde] Hey. Perfect timing.

1549
01:26:23,396 --> 01:26:24,937
- [door closes]
- I'm gonna go get a coffee.

1550
01:26:25,021 --> 01:26:26,437
Okay.

1551
01:26:26,521 --> 01:26:28,229
I'll be right back.

1552
01:26:30,104 --> 01:26:31,479
[door opens]

1553
01:26:31,562 --> 01:26:34,187
Oh. There she is.

1554
01:26:34,271 --> 01:26:37,104
Girl, I was high-key worried.

1555
01:26:37,187 --> 01:26:39,146
I would've come earlier,
but my boss made me

1556
01:26:39,229 --> 01:26:40,937
do, like, actual work.

1557
01:26:41,979 --> 01:26:44,687
You kept all this on the DL.

1558
01:26:44,771 --> 01:26:45,979
Ah?

1559
01:26:46,062 --> 01:26:48,604
Epilepsy and tubers?

1560
01:26:48,687 --> 01:26:50,812
Not to be confused with tumors,

1561
01:26:50,896 --> 01:26:53,187
although they sound just as shit.

1562
01:26:55,229 --> 01:26:56,937
I'm sorry for the secrets.

1563
01:26:57,021 --> 01:26:59,062
I get it.

1564
01:26:59,146 --> 01:27:00,979
You were looking for fun.

1565
01:27:01,062 --> 01:27:03,562
Which is why you gravitated to me. Hmm?

1566
01:27:06,562 --> 01:27:08,271
Speaking of fun, where's Prisha?

1567
01:27:08,354 --> 01:27:09,396
Is she here?

1568
01:27:09,479 --> 01:27:11,229
No.

1569
01:27:11,312 --> 01:27:14,312
All good things must come to an end.

1570
01:27:14,396 --> 01:27:15,479
She went home?

1571
01:27:15,562 --> 01:27:17,771
Yeah. But would I do it again?

1572
01:27:21,021 --> 01:27:22,271
Hell yeah, baby.

1573
01:27:24,312 --> 01:27:27,021
- [ticking]
- [monitor beeping steadily]

1574
01:27:52,187 --> 01:27:54,187
[gentle music playing]

1575
01:28:04,104 --> 01:28:05,687
[Julian] What happened?

1576
01:28:14,604 --> 01:28:15,812
Are you hurt?

1577
01:28:17,979 --> 01:28:20,146
I have tuberous sclerosis.

1578
01:28:22,062 --> 01:28:23,396
Causes epilepsy.

1579
01:28:24,687 --> 01:28:26,354
I was born with it.

1580
01:28:32,146 --> 01:28:34,354
What-what can we do?
Is there, is there a treatment?

1581
01:28:34,437 --> 01:28:36,896
Yes and no.

1582
01:28:36,979 --> 01:28:39,354
Medication helps,
but it's never been consistent.

1583
01:28:40,937 --> 01:28:43,437
And when I got here,
I stopped taking it altogether.

1584
01:28:43,521 --> 01:28:44,854
Why?

1585
01:28:46,437 --> 01:28:48,604
[voice breaking] Because it made me
feel numb.

1586
01:28:50,104 --> 01:28:52,854
Julian, I don't want to feel numb anymore.

1587
01:28:59,979 --> 01:29:01,646
Is surgery an option?

1588
01:29:01,729 --> 01:29:05,104
Yes, but there's too much risk.

1589
01:29:05,187 --> 01:29:06,896
I could lose my memory.

1590
01:29:14,271 --> 01:29:16,021
So...

1591
01:29:16,104 --> 01:29:18,521
so would that be the worst thing?

1592
01:29:18,604 --> 01:29:19,771
You would be healthy.

1593
01:29:21,187 --> 01:29:23,521
Everything I know would be gone.

1594
01:29:29,937 --> 01:29:32,146
Why didn't you tell me any of this?

1595
01:29:35,437 --> 01:29:38,312
Because I wanted to figure it out...

1596
01:29:39,479 --> 01:29:41,521
...for myself...

1597
01:29:43,062 --> 01:29:44,604
...what I'm living for.

1598
01:29:47,104 --> 01:29:49,021
And it's this place.

1599
01:29:52,229 --> 01:29:53,646
It's...

1600
01:29:55,312 --> 01:29:58,729
It's watching my mom do what she loves.

1601
01:29:59,771 --> 01:30:03,271
It's watching Amara
try a new makeup trend.

1602
01:30:05,729 --> 01:30:08,646
It's sitting in a dark cave with you...

1603
01:30:10,021 --> 01:30:13,479
...because you make darkness
feel peaceful.

1604
01:30:16,146 --> 01:30:18,104
Losing those memories...

1605
01:30:20,146 --> 01:30:22,729
...or the ability to make new ones...

1606
01:30:27,146 --> 01:30:29,146
...that's worse than death.

1607
01:30:33,729 --> 01:30:35,687
♪ ♪

1608
01:30:39,979 --> 01:30:42,479
[Julian breathes deeply]

1609
01:30:42,562 --> 01:30:44,312
I love you, Oriah.

1610
01:30:44,396 --> 01:30:45,604
[Ry chuckles]

1611
01:30:50,479 --> 01:30:52,396
[voice breaking] I love you, too.

1612
01:30:52,479 --> 01:30:54,479
♪ ♪

1613
01:31:12,021 --> 01:31:13,104
[sighs]

1614
01:31:16,979 --> 01:31:18,021
[sighs]

1615
01:31:19,396 --> 01:31:20,479
Ry?

1616
01:31:35,562 --> 01:31:36,771
[whispers] Ry.

1617
01:31:39,854 --> 01:31:41,646
Ry.

1618
01:31:44,937 --> 01:31:46,187
Ry.

1619
01:31:50,646 --> 01:31:51,854
Ry.

1620
01:31:53,312 --> 01:31:54,646
Ry!

1621
01:31:54,729 --> 01:31:56,229
No, no. Oriah!

1622
01:31:56,312 --> 01:31:57,521
Ry!

1623
01:32:01,729 --> 01:32:03,479
<i>Papá. Papá. Papá.</i>

1624
01:32:03,562 --> 01:32:05,562
[speaking urgently]

1625
01:32:08,979 --> 01:32:10,104
Ry, please.

1626
01:32:10,187 --> 01:32:12,187
[pensive music playing]

1627
01:32:16,187 --> 01:32:17,396
[EMT] Faint pulse.

1628
01:32:17,479 --> 01:32:18,812
She stopped breathing at the scene

1629
01:32:18,896 --> 01:32:20,812
- but stabilized in transport.
- Stay with me, okay?

1630
01:32:20,896 --> 01:32:22,729
I'm gonna be here, okay?

1631
01:32:22,812 --> 01:32:24,854
[doctor] <i>She's holding on, but barely.</i>

1632
01:32:24,937 --> 01:32:27,646
Scans show her condition has progressed.

1633
01:32:27,729 --> 01:32:31,146
It's your decision,
but we would strongly recommend surgery.

1634
01:32:34,396 --> 01:32:35,979
I mean, what is there to think about?

1635
01:32:36,062 --> 01:32:38,021
Ry has never wanted surgery.

1636
01:32:38,104 --> 01:32:41,729
I've tried to convince her for years,
and she made me promise.

1637
01:32:41,812 --> 01:32:45,646
We can stabilize her,
keep her comfortable.

1638
01:32:45,729 --> 01:32:48,354
But without surgery,
her condition will deteriorate,

1639
01:32:48,437 --> 01:32:51,021
and it will just be a matter of time.

1640
01:32:51,104 --> 01:32:53,104
Isolde...

1641
01:32:54,771 --> 01:32:57,187
...I understand the risks,

1642
01:32:57,271 --> 01:33:00,104
and Oriah spoke to me about her wishes.

1643
01:33:01,354 --> 01:33:05,562
But while there is a chance
that we could save her

1644
01:33:05,646 --> 01:33:08,146
and a chance she could have
a normal life...

1645
01:33:10,062 --> 01:33:12,896
...I beg you to take it.

1646
01:33:14,687 --> 01:33:18,812
She was worried about losing
the best parts of her life.

1647
01:33:19,854 --> 01:33:22,146
But if this works,

1648
01:33:22,229 --> 01:33:25,479
her favorite memories will be
the ones ahead of her.

1649
01:33:25,562 --> 01:33:27,521
♪ ♪

1650
01:33:41,437 --> 01:33:43,396
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1651
01:33:45,021 --> 01:33:46,979
[pensive music playing]

1652
01:34:05,562 --> 01:34:07,562
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1653
01:34:14,687 --> 01:34:17,521
[Isolde] She has the same condition
my mother had.

1654
01:34:18,562 --> 01:34:20,229
I'm so sorry, Izzy.

1655
01:34:24,896 --> 01:34:26,812
Does she know?

1656
